WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.400
Blind mating removes the need to reach the connection directly, but it

2
00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:06.540
doesn't remove the need to control alignment or electrical behavior.

3
00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.920
The equipment must reach the permitted mating condition, remain retained, and leave

4
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:12.520
that condition in a controlled way.

5
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:16.700
For the O R V three input interface, the specification describes use

6
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.480
of the power-sense line to control power-entry circuitry.

7
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:23.600
Equipment must not begin powering on before the connector is fully asserted,

8
00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:27.080
and it must power off before removal to prevent arcing events.

9
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.880
This is a requirement-level sequence, not an instruction to reproduce an unspecified

10
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:32.680
internal circuit.

11
00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:37.360
Check the equipment implementation against the actual connector and power-entry requirements.

12
00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:42.680
Don't infer a particular precharge circuit, contact timing or safe live-service procedure

13
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:43.940
from a conceptual sequence.

14
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:49.560
Connector and power-monitoring specifications provide supporting detail, but the rack-level decision is

15
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.720
whether the selected interfaces and controls establish the required behavior together.

16
00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:56.080
Mechanical fit alone can't prove it.

17
00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:59.940
The responsible electrical review and qualification remain necessary.

